CORE
ct3.sv

^\[main\.p0\] always main\.cnt <= 255: PROVED \(transition property\)$
^\[main\.p1\] main\.cnt == 0: PROVED \(CT=0\)$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A state-predicate property (p1, CT=0) must be proved unbounded even when
another property (p0) with a larger completeness threshold is present. The
completeness-threshold engine must compare the bound reached against each
property's own threshold, not against the maximum threshold over all
properties.
